  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tropical Cyclone Pam Recovery Package</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 13 March 2015, Tropical Cyclone Pam struck Vanuatu, affecting 195,000 people and causing damage and losses equivalent to 64 per cent of the island state&#x2019;s Gross Domestic Product. The recovery program supports the objectives under the Government of Vanuatu&apos;s National Cyclone Recovery and Economic Strengthening Program. The program&apos;s End-of-program outcomes are: Improved health and education facilities through restored buildings in select communities; Improved public service delivery through restored buildings in select communities; Improved livelihoods through increased skills and market access opportunities in select communities; and improved disaster preparedness through increased knowledge of protection issues among vulnerable groups in select communities.</narrative>
  </description>
